Subject: [PATCH] zune-jpeg: size the upsampler scratch from the widest component

HV upsampling scratch was sized from components[0] only, so a component with
a wider stride trips the upsample_hv assertion. The other hunks turn panics on
the same malformed layouts into errors or skips: a progressive colorspace with
more components than the SOF, an MCU row shorter than the vertical upsampler
expects, and a 1x1 IDCT into a too-short output tail. Each was hit through
image's JPEG decoder; the test added here decodes one input per hunk and
fails without the fix (scalar and AVX2 paths).

Upstream: the scratch sizing is fixed by etemesi254/zune-image#374 (36007420,
"jpeg: fix scratch space for baseline and progressive upsampling"). zune-image
main (2cdbbf5 and HEAD 692520a) decodes all four test inputs without
panicking, but no release has that code: 0.5.15 is the latest stable, and
0.5.16-rc3 (crates.io, 2026-10-19) still panics on the vertical upsample input
(worker.rs:470). The `rchunks`/`worker.rs` guards here overlap the zune-image
project's fix-jpeg-{mcu,worker}-upsampling-bounds.patch.

diff --git a/src/idct/scalar.rs b/src/idct/scalar.rs
index 624e2c8..023b4c1 100644
--- a/src/idct/scalar.rs
+++ b/src/idct/scalar.rs
@@ -29,6 +29,14 @@ fn wm(a: i32, b: i32) -> i32 {
 
 #[inline]
 pub fn idct_int_1x1(in_vector: &mut [i32; 64], mut out_vector: &mut [i16], stride: usize) {
+    // `mcu` can pass an empty or too-short tail slice from `get_mut(idct_position..)`; skip writes
+    // rather than panicking (full IDCT already uses a temp-buffer fallback for short outputs).
+    let Some(min_out) = stride.checked_mul(7).and_then(|n| n.checked_add(8)) else {
+        return;
+    };
+    if out_vector.len() < min_out {
+        return;
+    }
     let coeff = ((wa(wa(in_vector[0], 4), 1024) >> 3).clamp(0, 255)) as i16;
 
     out_vector[..8].fill(coeff);
